@file ComparatorChallenges/BenjaminiSchramm.lean
@decl OAI.Percolation.BenjaminiSchramm.cayley_main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The Benjamini–Schramm nonuniqueness conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves the nonuniqueness phase conjecture for Bernoulli bond percolation on infinite connected locally finite nonamenable quasi-transitive graphs. It establishes $p_c<p_{2\to2}\le p_u$ and a common nonempty coupled interval with infinitely many infinite clusters almost surely. For Cayley graphs, the result holds for every finite symmetric generating set of a nonamenable finitely generated group and every $p\in(p_c,p_u)$. The selected critical estimates include a finite triangle diagram, susceptibility of order $(p_c-p)^{-1}$, percolation probability of order $p-p_c$, cluster-volume tail of order $n^{-1/2}$, and intrinsic and extrinsic radius tails of order $n^{-1}$. Connection probabilities decay exponentially below $p_{2\to2}$.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Probability.BenjaminiSchramm.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

