@file ComparatorChallenges/CannonGeometricAction.lean
@decl OAI.CannonRelease.cannon
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Cannon's conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: Cannon's conjecture asks whether a hyperbolic group with boundary homeomorphic to the two-sphere acts geometrically on hyperbolic three-space. The formalization proves that such a group admits an isometric action on $\mathbb H^3$ that is proper and cocompact and has finite kernel. Hyperbolicity is expressed through uniformly thin geodesic triangles in a Cayley graph, and the boundary hypothesis is a homeomorphism with $S^2$.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Geometry.Cannon.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

