-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result gives a logarithmic improvement in the independence number of clique-free graphs. For every fixed integer $r\ge4$, there is $c_r>0$ such that every finite $K_r$-free simple graph on $n$ vertices with average degree $d\ge2$ has an independent set of size at least $c_r n\log d/d$. The constant depends only on $r$.
