@file ComparatorChallenges/CoarseAssembly.lean
@decl OAI.CoarseAssembly.bounded_geometry_graph_counterexample_unconditional
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Failure of rational injectivity for maximal coarse assembly
-- L4DEL: intuition: The coarse Novikov conjecture predicts rational injectivity of the ordinary coarse assembly map for uniformly discrete spaces of bounded geometry. The formalization constructs a counterexample from a coarse disjoint union of finite connected graphs with uniformly bounded degree. Its degree-one coarse $K$-homology contains an infinite-order class whose image under ordinary coarse assembly into the reduced locally compact Roe algebra vanishes. The class remains nonzero after tensoring with $\mathbb Q$, so rational injectivity fails.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
