@file ComparatorChallenges/CoveringDensity.lean
@decl OAI.CoveringOrder.optimal_order
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The optimal order of convex-body covering density
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result gives an absolute constant $C>0$ such that every convex body $K\subset\mathbb R^n$, $n\ge2$, admits a covering by translates along one full-rank lattice $L$ with density $|K|/\mathrm{covol}(L)\le Cn\log n$. The covering is exact, and no symmetry, boundary regularity, or volume normalization is assumed. The formalization determines the order of the largest covering density in dimension $n$. For all sufficiently large $n$, the suprema of translative covering density and lattice covering density are each bounded above and below by absolute positive multiples of $n\log n$, both over all convex bodies and over centrally symmetric convex bodies.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Geometry.CoveringDensity.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

