@file ComparatorChallenges/CriticalPercolation.lean
@decl OAI.CriticalPercolation.BondGraph.no_percolation_at_criticality
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Critical percolation on every quasi-transitive graph
-- L4DEL: intuition: The critical-percolation question asks whether an infinite cluster can remain at the threshold. The formalized result proves that, at their respective critical probabilities, nearest-neighbor bond and site percolation on $\mathbb Z^3$ almost surely have no infinite cluster. Equivalently, almost surely every vertex belongs to a finite cluster in each model. The formalization proves absence of an infinite cluster at criticality for Bernoulli bond percolation on every infinite connected locally finite quasi-transitive graph with critical probability $p_c<1$. At $p=p_c$, the probability that any infinite cluster exists is zero. The graph model permits bond multiplicities.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Probability.CriticalPercolation.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

