@file ComparatorChallenges/Dixmier.lean
@decl OAI.Dixmier.main_theorem_all_universes
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Amenability, unitarizability, and strong Ulam stability
-- L4DEL: intuition: Dixmier's unitarizability problem asks whether a discrete group is amenable exactly when every uniformly bounded Hilbert-space representation is similar to a unitary one. The formalization establishes this equivalence for every discrete group. For every nonamenable group and every $\varepsilon>0$, it also gives a nonunitarizable representation with uniform operator bound at most $1+\varepsilon$. The Hilbert space can be chosen separable for countable groups; a separate linked statement records a separable witness with uniform bound $101$ in that case.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.Unitarizability.UniverseTransport as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

