@decl OAI.HarmonicCounterexample.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Failure of integer-degree harmonic dimension comparison
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result disproves the proposed Euclidean upper comparison for dimensions of harmonic functions with integer polynomial growth. It constructs one complete smooth metric with nonnegative Ricci curvature on an even-dimensional Euclidean space, Euclidean near the origin and with asymptotic volume ratio strictly between zero and one, admitting more independent harmonic functions of the prescribed growth degree than the Euclidean count. The construction uses dimension $16$ and degree $50000$. Separate tangent-cone and cone-spectrum conclusions are not included.
