@file ComparatorChallenges/KadisonRingrose.lean
@decl OAI.BoundedHochschild.KadisonRingrose.main_result
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The Kadison–Ringrose cohomology conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves vanishing of bounded Hochschild cohomology in every degree at least two for a complex von Neumann algebra with coefficients in itself. Every bounded multilinear cocycle of such a degree is the Hochschild differential of a bounded multilinear cochain one degree lower. No separability or type restriction is imposed. The degree-one inner-derivation theorem is outside this selected statement.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.BoundedHochschild.MainResult as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/KadisonSimilarity.lean
@decl OAI.KadisonSimilarity.similarityTheorem
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Kadison's similarity conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: Kadison's similarity problem asks whether every bounded unital homomorphism from a unital complex $C^*$-algebra into operators on a Hilbert space is similar to a $*$-homomorphism. The formalization proves this for arbitrary Hilbert spaces. It also gives one universal hyperreflexivity constant for all unital von Neumann algebras. The linked commutator estimate is uniform over all finite matrix amplifications: its constant is independent of the algebra, Hilbert space, and amplification size. This is the quantitative derivation estimate supporting the similarity result.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.KadisonSimilarity.UnconditionalSimilarity as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

