@file ComparatorChallenges/KLInvariance.lean
@decl OAI.KLInvariance.combinatorial_invariance
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Combinatorial invariance of Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomials
-- L4DEL: intuition: The combinatorial invariance conjecture asks whether a Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomial depends only on its Bruhat interval as an ordered set. The formalization proves that every order isomorphism between Bruhat intervals in arbitrary Coxeter systems preserves the corresponding equal-parameter Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomial. The two intervals may come from different Coxeter systems.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.RepresentationTheory.KazhdanLusztig.Invariance as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

