@file ComparatorChallenges/ListHadwiger.lean
@decl OAI.LinearListHadwiger.main_theorem
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Graph coloring, clique minors, and Colin de Verdière invariants
-- L4DEL: intuition: Hadwiger's conjecture predicts $\chi(G)\le h(G)$ for every finite graph, where $h(G)$ is the largest clique-minor order. The formalization constructs arbitrarily large finite simple counterexamples with independence number at most two. For a graph on $m$ vertices it proves $h(G)<26m/75+2/3<m/2\le\chi(G)$. This disproves the ordinary chromatic form. The paper's fractional-chromatic strengthening and the Colin de Verdière consequence are outside this selected statement. The Linear List Hadwiger conjecture asks for a universal linear bound on list chromatic number in terms of clique-minor size. The formalization proves that there is one integer $C\ge1$ such that every finite nonempty simple graph $G$ satisfies $\chi_{\mathrm{list}}(G)\le C h(G)$, where $h(G)$ is the largest order of a clique minor. The constant is independent of the graph.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Combinatorics.ListHadwiger.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/LittleFinitistic.lean
@decl OAI.LittleFinitistic.Main.exists_counterexample
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: A counterexample to finitistic-dimension finiteness
-- L4DEL: intuition: The little finitistic-dimension conjecture predicts that finitely generated modules of finite projective dimension over a fixed finite-dimensional algebra have bounded projective dimensions. The formalized counterexample is a finite-dimensional complex algebra with a finitely generated module of projective dimension at least $2m-2$ and still finite for every $m\ge1$. A separate formalized result gives a finite-dimensional complex algebra whose little and big finitistic dimensions are infinite on the left and zero on the right. Injectives fail to generate its unbounded derived category on the left and generate it on the right.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Algebra.Finitistic.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

