@file ComparatorChallenges/PiExponent.lean
@decl OAI.PiExponent.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The irrationality exponent of π is 2
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves that the irrationality exponent of $\pi$ is exactly two. For every $\nu>2$, all sufficiently large positive denominators $q$ satisfy $|\pi-p/q|\ge q^{-\nu}$ for every integer numerator $p$. It also states the exact supremum characterization using infinitely many rational approximations. The paper's convergence consequence for the Flint–Hills series is outside this selected statement.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
