@file ComparatorChallenges/SLELowerPositivity.lean
@decl OAI.SLEExactGauge.sourceLowerMain_proved
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Exact Hausdorff gauges for SLE
-- L4DEL: intuition: For $0<\kappa<8$, put $d=1+\kappa/8$. The formalization proves that every continuous nondecreasing Hausdorff gauge agreeing with $h(r)=r^d(\log\log(1/r))^{(2-d)/2}$ at sufficiently small positive radii almost surely assigns positive measure to every nontrivial compact positive-time segment of ordinary chordal $\mathrm{SLE}_\kappa$.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Probability.SLE.LowerPositivity as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/SmoothInitialForm.lean
@decl OAI.PermanentBorder.smooth_initial_form_lower_bound
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: A cubic permanent–determinant lower bound
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves a cubic lower bound for both exact and border determinantal representations of the complex $m\times m$ permanent. For $m\ge1408$, every affine-linear determinant representation of size $n$, including coefficientwise limits, satisfies $n\ge m^3/(5529600e)$. A general supporting theorem applies to a polynomial in $d\ge2$ variables whose first nonzero homogeneous Taylor term has degree $r\ge2$ and no nonzero singular zero. Its exact and border determinantal sizes are at least $(r-1)(d-1)/(4e)$. The paper's algebraic-branching-program consequences are outside these statements.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Algebra.Determinantal.InitialForm as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

