@file ComparatorChallenges/SteinitzBergstrom.lean
@decl OAI.EuclideanSteinitzBergstrom.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The Euclidean Steinitz–Bergström bound
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalized result gives the Euclidean Steinitz–Bergström bound with one absolute constant $C$. For every finite family of vectors in the unit ball of $\mathbb R^d$, signs can be chosen so that every prefix in the prescribed order has norm at most $C\sqrt d$. When the vector sum is zero, a permutation makes every unsigned prefix satisfy the same bound. Repeated and zero vectors are included. The result is existential and does not supply an online algorithm.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.Steinitz.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/StrictMeans.lean
@decl OAI.StrictInverseFirstPower.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Brennan's conjecture and the integral-means spectrum
-- L4DEL: intuition: Brennan's conjecture asserts that $|\phi'|^s$ is area-integrable for $4/30$ and the spectrum value $B_{\mathcal S}(-2)=1$. The Koebe map and its inverse give divergence at all four boundary exponents. Kraetzer's proposed integral-means spectrum predicts $B_b(-1)=1/4$ for bounded univalent maps. The formalized result proves $B_b(-1)<1/4$, contradicting that prediction. The underlying estimate gives constants $0<\varepsilon<1/4$ and $C<\infty$ such that the normalized circular mean of $|f'|^{-1}$ is at most $C(1-r)^{-1/4+\varepsilon}$ for every normalized univalent disk map and $1/2\le r<1$. The bound requires neither bounded image nor boundary regularity, and no numerical value of $\varepsilon$ is specified.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.StrictMeans.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/StrongKadisonKastler.lean
@decl OAI.KadisonKastler.universal_strong_stability
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Strong Kadison–Kastler stability and its spatial boundaries
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves the strong Kadison–Kastler conjecture uniformly. For every $\varepsilon>0$, there is a $\delta>0$ such that any two unital von Neumann algebras on the same complex Hilbert space at Kadison–Kastler distance below $\delta$ are conjugate by a unitary $u$ with $\lVert u-1\rVert<\varepsilon$. The tolerance depends only on $\varepsilon$, uniformly over the algebras, their representations, and the Hilbert space.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Analysis.KadisonKastler.StrongStability as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

@file ComparatorChallenges/StronglyRayleighDPP.lean
@decl OAI.Problem336AdditiveD139.countable_positive_contraction_dpp_exists_unique
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: The free uniform spanning forest is a factor of IID
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves that the free uniform spanning forest is a factor of independent identically distributed vertex labels on every infinite connected locally finite simple unweighted graph. One Borel equivariant rule works for all such graphs and uses no distinguished root. The linked supplements also give equivariant IID sampling for invariant strongly Rayleigh laws on countable groups and existence, uniqueness, and IID-factor results for determinantal laws with Hermitian positive-contraction kernels on countable index sets. These group results require neither amenability nor finite generation, and the kernels need not be trace class.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Probability.StrongRayleigh.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

