@file ComparatorChallenges/TorsionFreeZeroDivisors.lean
@decl OAI.TorsionFreeZeroDivisors.main
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: A counterexample to Kaplansky’s zero-divisor conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: Kaplansky's zero-divisor conjecture asserts that the group algebra of a torsion-free group over a field has no zero divisors. The formalized result constructs a finitely presented torsion-free group $G$ and nonzero elements $\alpha,\beta\in\mathbb F_2[G]$ with $\alpha\beta=0$, giving a counterexample. The same group admits a finite two-dimensional classifying space $K(G,1)$.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.Algebra.GroupRing.Main as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

