@file ComparatorChallenges/TotientAsymptotic.lean
@decl OAI.TotientAsymptotic.coefficient_nonnegative
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: An asymptotic formula for the number of totients
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $V(x)$ count the distinct values of Euler's totient function up to $x$. The formalization constructs the paper's explicit positive main term from finite arithmetic approximants and proves that their ratio tends to one. In particular, $V(cx)/V(x)\to c$ for every fixed $c>0$, answering the Erdős–Hall regular-variation question. The formalization also gives asymptotics for totients $v\le x$ whose least preimage $\ell(v)=\min\{n\ge1:\varphi(n)=v\}$ lies between $kx$ and $(k+1)x$. The associated coefficient is positive under the stated existence condition; when no totient $d$ satisfies $kd<\ell(d)$, the count and coefficient are identically zero. The cases $k=1,2$ have positive coefficients.
-- L4DEL: step: This is an exact comparator target linked by the pinned repository's formalization note for this result.
-- L4DEL: step: The repository's comparator configuration selects OAI.NumberTheory.TotientAsymptotic.UnconditionalMain as the released solution module checked against this declaration.

