@decl OAI.PureTypeSystem.weak_implies_strong
-- L4DEL: title: Challenge statement: Weak normalization implies strong normalization in pure type systems
-- L4DEL: intuition: The formalization proves the $\beta$-Barendregt–Geuvers–Klop conjecture for pure type systems: if every legal expression in every valid context has some terminating $\beta$-reduction sequence, then every $\beta$-reduction sequence from every such expression terminates. Reduction is allowed inside type annotations, and the specification may have arbitrary sorts and nonfunctional axioms or rules.
